The copy is kept in step with the protobuf-net the server serializes with. Upgrading that
library means re-reading this file against the upstream tree the new version was built from,
taking the new copy if it changed, and updating the two lines below. Nothing can compare the
copy to its original automatically, because there is no original to fetch from the package --
so VendoredBclSchemaShould in tests/Avalon.Shared.UnitTests fails on the upgrade instead,
which is the moment that reading is worth doing.

